WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauding)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Kejal] Venezuela unveiled

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.870
its new national map in December,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.813
adding an area the size of
Florida to its territory.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.400
But this land called the
Essequibo belongs to Guyana,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.710
a country rich in golden diamonds,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.090
it is now one of the world's

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.330
fastest growing crude oil producers.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.680
For more than a century,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.615
Venezuela has laid claim to the Territory

00:00:22.615 --> 00:00:25.060
- Annexing Essequibo practically

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.303
wiping Guyana off of the map.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.250
- I'm here in Caracas,

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.370
trying to understand more
about President Maduro's plans

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:36.210
to take over this land and
what it means in this region

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.213
as these two oil-rich countries clash.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.710
- [Kejal] The dispute for the Essequibo

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.990
dates back to the 19th century

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.970
when Great Britain acquired Guyana

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.580
and expanded its Territory to the West.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.160
But Venezuela protested
saying the Essequibo

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.923
was part of its Territory
under Spanish rule.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.870
Tensions between the two
countries intensified in 1966

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.990
when Guyana gained
independence from Britain.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.000
Guyana has since sought a resolution

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.070
through the International
Court of Justice,

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.083
but Venezuela rejects the procedure.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.640
The Essequibo makes up
two thirds of Guyana

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.100
and is mostly covered in rainforest.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.970
The Territory has large
reserves of gold and diamonds

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.650
- Essequibo region contribute

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.740
to the country's economic wealth.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.740
Our forest is an important resource.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.923
We have large deposits of gold reserves,

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.370
- [Kejal] But a turning point came in 2015

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.983
when oil was found off
the Essequibo Coast.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.275
Since then, a consortium

00:01:40.275 --> 00:01:43.440
led by the US Oil giant, ExxonMobil,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.770
said it has discovered up
to 11 billion barrels of oil

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.020
and natural gas resources.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.670
Oil executives say that

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.250
this was the largest
discovery of the decade.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.640
It could give the country the
highest oil output per capita

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.123
in the world ahead of oil-rich
Kuwait and Saudi Arabia.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:05.160
- Guyana it's interesting
because it is a new producer.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.350
It's a country where until 2015,

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.150
no one knew that there was oil

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.021
and it has started to produce,

00:02:10.021 --> 00:02:13.260
and it's a not OPEC member,
which is very important.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.530
And it includes it's
possibility to already

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.666
deliver oil to the market in
a market that is restricted

00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:23.253
because of all the sanctions
that exist to Russia.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.940
- [Kejal] Because of its
new found oil revenues,

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.790
Guyana had the highest real GDP growth

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.410
in the world in 2022, 62.3%,

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:36.532
and the International Monetary Fund

00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:39.393
predicts its GDP will keep growing.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:44.460
Guyana went from one of South
America's poorest countries

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.520
to having one of the world's
fastest growing economies.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.720
- We are poised to earn,

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.463
on average about 5 to $6
billion per annum by 2035.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.510
- But Venezuela's president Nicolas Maduro

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.790
says the oil reserves in the Essequibo

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.413
belong to his country.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.010
While Guyana reaps from the oil windfall.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.710
Venezuela's economy has contracted 80%

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.383
since Maduro came to office in 2013.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.000
Nearly 8 million Venezuelans
have fled in the past decade.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.763
Hundreds of thousands of
them wound up in the US.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.260
In order to oust Maduro,
the US imposed sanctions

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.113
on the Venezuelan oil industry in 2019.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.860
The Biden administration
agreed to temporarily lift

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.040
some economic sanctions
on Venezuela in October

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.230
in exchange for democratic reforms,

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.870
which include allowing
opposition candidates

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.070
to run in this year's
presidential election.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.104
US officials said that
allowing more oil and gas money

00:03:43.104 --> 00:03:45.683
to flow in could help stabilize Venezuela

00:03:45.683 --> 00:03:48.363
and ease the large flow of migrants.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.110
But when it comes to
the Essequibo dispute,

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.660
Washington is not a Venezuela side.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.060
The State Department
said it supports Guyana,

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.350
which has held meetings

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.630
with officials from the
US Defense Department

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.203
to increase cooperation.

00:04:02.203 --> 00:04:04.170
(groovy music)

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.060
In December, Venezuela's government

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.920
said more than 10 million voters

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.716
approved annexing
Essequibo in a referendum.

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:13.795
(protestor speaking in foreign language)

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:15.450
(drum music)

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.640
But election experts have cast doubts

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.383
on the veracity of the results,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.620
especially in a country
where the government

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.590
has been accused of
widespread electoral fraud

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.169
in past elections.

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:31.752
(Maduro speaking in foreign language)

00:04:44.736 --> 00:04:46.140
- [Kejal] After the referendum,

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.080
Maduro ordered the country's
state-owned companies

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.750
to explore and exploit the oil, gas,

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.970
and mines in the Essequibo,

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.965
and told foreign companies
that they have three months

00:04:55.965 --> 00:04:59.130
to abandon their operations in the region.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.520
- Guyana views this as an imminent trap

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.590
to its territorial integrity

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:08.040
and will intensify precautionary measures.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.080
- [Kejal] As tension started to rise,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.990
the UK sent a warship to support Guyana

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.280
and Maduro responded

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.643
with air and naval
exercises near the border.

00:05:19.637 --> 00:05:21.720
(cheerful music)

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.730
Experts said the referendum was largely

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.713
a wag the dog moment for Maduro,

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.418
as he tries to rally nationalist support

00:05:28.418 --> 00:05:31.443
ahead of the presidential
election later this year.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.730
- It's a typical strategy
of a dictator autocrat

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:40.500
of finding a problem to distract
people from their reality,

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.860
which is a completely
devastated economic situation

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.113
and a horrible humanitarian situation.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.930
- [Kejal] The leaders of Guyana

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.375
and Venezuela have met
to discuss the annexation

00:05:51.375 --> 00:05:54.390
and agreed to avoid conflict,

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:57.690
but Guyana refused Maud's
plans to settle the dispute

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:02.220
through bilateral negotiations
asking the UN to intervene

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.563
and lay Venezuela's claims to rest.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.189
But experts say the case is
likely to drag on for years.

00:06:09.189 --> 00:06:11.856
(pensive music)

